2	 "gdd": "design/gdd/save-load-and-versioned-format.md",
3	 "blockers": [
4	  {
5	   "where": "SL-2 (line 181, allowed-type sentence) vs AC-SL-07 (line 1169) and ADR-0006 section 1.2 item 3",
6	   "issue": "The diff changed AC-SL-07 so PackedFloat32Array, PackedFloat64Array and PackedStringArray are refused (SL_PRECHECK_BLOCK_TYPE_FORBIDDEN). The normative rule in SL-2 was not changed. It still reads 'allowed are null, bool, int, float, String, Array, Dictionary and the packed arrays (the H7 set, kernel CR-14)' and its forbidden list omits those three types. SL-2 also never says non-finite floats are rejected, which ADR-0006 section 1.2 and Implementation Guidelines require. An implementer reading SL-2 would accept float and string packed arrays, and AC-SL-07 would then fail.",
7	   "fix": "Rewrite the allowed set in SL-2 to: null, bool, int (full 64 bits), finite float, String, Array, Dictionary with String or int keys, and PackedByteArray / PackedInt32Array / PackedInt64Array only. Add PackedFloat32Array, PackedFloat64Array, PackedStringArray and non-finite floats to the forbidden list. Add a NaN/inf case to AC-SL-07. Make the 'H7 set, kernel CR-14' citation say 'narrowed by ADR-0006 1.2'."
8	  },
9	  {
10	   "where": "AC-SL-38 (line 1228), Tuning Knobs preamble (line 992), OQ-28 (line 1459)",
11	   "issue": "The range check was demoted to an ADVISORY safe-range diff (ADR-0007 2.5), and the rest of the text still assumes it is a refusing first layer. (a) AC-SL-38 Layer 1 now boots AUTOSAVE_RETRY_TICKS = 0 with only an advisory, since 0 is within declared int width. The I3 invariant takes (W_MIN_WARNING_S x TICK_RATE) mod R, so it would run a modulo by zero. Lines 992 and 1459 claim 'no invariant ever divides by an out-of-bound knob', but the GDD declares no schema bounds (lo/hi) for any knob. (b) The 'Rows added' sentence in the same AC still says 'LOSS_CEILING_TICKS 11 399 refused by the range check'. (c) The AC title and Layer 1 label still read 'knob ranges first ... (runs first, OQ-28 decided)'.",
12	   "fix": "Add a hard schema-bound column to the Tuning Knobs table, or a short list. It must give lo >= 1 for every divisor or modulus knob (AUTOSAVE_RETRY_TICKS, TICK_RATE and the others the I-series divide by). Make AC-SL-38 assert RETRY_TICKS 0 refuses CONTENT_FIELD_RANGE, while the other Layer 1 values (901, 5 399, 18 001, 3 601, 15 KiB, 11 399) boot with an advisory. Reword the 11 399 row and the AC title and Layer 1 label to match."
13	  },
14	  {
15	   "where": "AC-SL-24 (line 1206) vs SL-9 (line 209) and AC-SL-70 / AC-SL-116",
16	   "issue": "SL-9 now defers the whole PROFILE file mechanism (profile.sav write, ring of one, .bak, change-detection trigger) to the first PROFILE block, not before Alpha. AC-SL-70 and AC-SL-116 were marked deferred. AC-SL-24, an MVP kill-during-write criterion, still requires kill points 'at each of the same points of a profile.sav write'. No profile writer exists at MVP, so that clause cannot be tested and may push an implementer into building the deferred writer.",
17	   "fix": "Mark the profile.sav clause of AC-SL-24 as deferred with SL-9, as was done for AC-SL-70 and AC-SL-116. Keep the WORLD-generation kill matrix at MVP."
18	  }
